# Develop [[.Name]]

Work from the project root. Read `project.json` and `main_test.go` first.
Discover the actual admin API in the host project before inventing new endpoints.
If an endpoint is missing, implement it in that project's existing stack, reusing
its authentication and authorisation. Keep business logic on the server.

The pinned runtime supports GET, string query inputs and unary JSON responses.
Map input names to API query names in `http.query`. Do not silently represent a
write as GET or invent manifest fields. A capability outside this contract needs
an SDK extension or upgrade before the project can use it.

Add or change a fixture test alongside each command. Cover the exact request path,
query encoding, auth requirements, successful result and relevant failure. Keep
tests offline with `httptest`, and never use a real token. `main_test.go` also builds
and executes the native CLI so the embedded manifest is tested.

Run `go mod tidy`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...`. `go run . describe` exposes
the actual command contract without credentials. If Loop is installed, use
`loop check --manifest project.json` and `loop run --manifest project.json -- describe`.

Configuration names are `[[.BaseURLEnv]]` and `[[.TokenEnv]]`. Do not read their
values merely for discovery or put them in diagnostics. Keep the dependency in
`go.mod` pinned and update `.loop/scaffold.json` when deliberately upgrading it.
